<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qusayy ibn Kilab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qusayy ibn <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kilab">Kilab</a> was, according to Arab tradition, the leader who gathered the scattered clans of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in the 5th century and won control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a> from the Khuza'a. He organised the pilgrimage and founded the Dar al-Nadwa, the council house of Mecca. He was an ancestor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a>.</p></div>
